<p>Most design systems hand an AI a screenshot and hope. This one hands it two things it can actually use.</p>

<h2>The skill</h2>
<p><code>skills/im-design-system/SKILL.md</code> is an <a href="https://skills.sh/">agent skill</a>: the rules (three layers of tokens, the two states, words over a picture, Ghost's reserved helper names, provenance), the page shapes, the helpers that always ship, the motion tokens and how to make other things in the look — everything an assistant needs to <em>know</em> before it writes a line. Install it into any agent that reads skills:</p>
{{{{code "bash"}}}}
npx skills add https://github.com/imswarnil/Swarnil-Design-System --skill im-design-system
{{{{/code}}}}

<h2>The MCP server</h2>
<p><code>mcp/server.mjs</code> lets the assistant <em>look</em>. It reads this repository at call time, so it can never describe a component that has changed — and every colour, duration and curve it quotes is read from the tokens, never typed.</p>
{{{{code "json"}}}}
{ "mcpServers": { "im-design-system": { "command": "node", "args": ["/path/to/design.imswarnil.com/mcp/server.mjs"] } } }
{{{{/code}}}}

